<style type="text/css">
.pl-about { color: #1d2935; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; margin: 0 auto; max-width: 76rem; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
.pl-about a { color: #064d93; }
.pl-about a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #003399; outline-offset: 2px; }
.pl-about p { font-size: .9rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: .85rem 0; }
.pl-about-credits { margin: 1.2rem 0; }
.pl-about-credits h2 { color: #17212b; font-size: 1rem; margin: 0 0 .5rem; }
.pl-about-credit-list { border-top: 1px solid #b6c5d2; list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
.pl-about-credit-list li { border-bottom: 1px solid #cbd6de; font-size: .86rem; line-height: 1.5; padding: .5rem .15rem; }
.pl-about-credit-list span { color: #526170; }
.pl-about-history { border-top: 1px solid #b6c5d2; padding-top: .2rem; }
</style>

<div class="pl-about">
  [% INCLUDE modernboxheader.tt title = 'The Physics Library Story' %]
  <p>Just as Physics would not exist without math, so also Physics Library would not exist without <a href="https://www.planetmath.org">PlanetMath</a>.</p>

  <section class="pl-about-credits" aria-labelledby="about-credits-heading">
    <h2 id="about-credits-heading">Some credits:</h2>
    <ul class="pl-about-credit-list">
      <li><strong>Aaron Krowne</strong><span> - design, coding</span></li>
      <li><strong>Ben Loftin</strong><span> - PlanetPhysics and Physics Library setup, testing, coding</span></li>
      <li><strong>Logan Hanks</strong><span> - coding</span></li>
      <li><strong>Joel Irby</strong><span> - coding</span></li>
      <li><strong>Nathan Egge</strong><span> - design, coding</span></li>
      <li><strong>djao</strong><span> - licensing, testing, content</span></li>
      <li><strong>ink</strong><span> - original logo</span></li>
      <li><strong>zoner</strong><span> - new logo</span></li>
      <li><strong>joe s.</strong><span> - initial hosting</span></li>
      <li><strong>drini</strong><span> - testing, content</span></li>
      <li><strong>Yuxin Chen</strong><span> - computer admin</span></li>
      <li><strong>undernet #math</strong><span> - moral support!</span></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <div class="pl-about-history">
    <p>Physics Library was initially PlanetPhysics and was hosted in Blacksburg, VA, with the Virginia Tech <a href="https://www.dlib.vt.edu">Digital Library Research Lab</a> in the <a href="https://www.cc.vt.edu">Computing Center</a>.</p>
  </div>
</div>
